ainty high", "R+4 district offset by a favorable Democratic environment; Trump's Fort Myers rally aids GOP turnout"], "rationale": "Most professional raters call this open seat a tossup, while markets, Dandiya's large cash advantage, and outside spending against Askar tilt it slightly Democratic despite the district's Republican lean. With no fresh polling to confirm either direction, a small Democratic edge with wide uncertainty fits the evidence.", "watch": "Fresh public polling or a visible turnout shift around Trump's Fort Myers rally could move the race toward either nominee.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 48 days old; polling uncertainty inflated."]}, "overview": "Florida's 22nd District is an open seat that leans Republican on paper, but the contest between Republican Casey Askar and Democrat Pia Dandiya is rated a tossup by most professional raters. Prediction markets give Dandiya a modest edge, and the fundamentals point slightly her way, with a favorable national environment offsetting the district's Republican lean.\n\nThe polling record is thin and stale, with the newest public survey from late August showing a two-point Democratic edge. Dandiya holds a large cash-on-hand advantage and benefits from outside advertising opposing Askar, who has relied heavily on self-funding and ends the quarter with little cash. A Trump rally in Fort Myers could sharpen Republican turnout in the stretch run. The seat remains genuinely competitive, with only a slight Democratic tilt.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.5161, "margin": 0.22}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4293, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5493, "margin": 0.2}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.5402, "margin": 0.2}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4658, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4995, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.5432, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.5455, "margin": 0.2}, {"date